Documentation for GKupload V4.06
                  Written By Gregory M. Kerr 13 of April 1993


Synopsis:

    Gkupload is a file maintenance program to be used with TransAmiga1.1
    major features:
                1] read TransAmiga configuration files to find library
                   names, Paths to file areas and the Sysop's name

                2] if a file does not have a description GKupload will ask
                   for a comment and will then write a desc file and add a
                   filenote to this file.

                3] it will remember any uploader and the comments already
                   made by the Uploader.

                4] so many other features that I can't remember them all.

                5] Added code to create a list for each area, This allows
                   the writing of a script to create a files list for
                   download within TransAmiga.


Usage:

    Place file GKupload in your rexx: directory then if you type 'rx
    GKupload ?' you will be presented with a help screen like this:

         Usage rx GKUpload <[*]|[Area Number]|[?]> [MAGIC] [OVERNIGHT]

                   * = Process all valid TransAmiga1.1 file areas.
         Area Number = Any valid area number up to highest area number.
                   ? = This help.
                  -M = Create magic files list.
                  -O = Overnight switch using this automatically adds comment.

         All switches are optional but if using the overnight switch then it
         must always be last.

         Written By Gregory M. Kerr. on the 13 of April 1993
               This is version 4.06

        Rather self explanatory really but if you need more help here we go.
    If you use the '*' wildcard the program will read your
    'BBS:configs/file.cfg' file to find out how many file areas that you
    have, the names of the file areas(Library names) and the paths for each
    file area. It will then process each area checking the original
    files.bbs with the new directory listing if the file is the same the
    information gets passed to the new listing. If the file is not the same
    then it receives further processing. The net result is that you end up
    with a new files.bbs for every area in your BBS.

        If you wish you can also specify a specific file area by number the
    only difference here is that GKUpload will only process this area. The
    number is checked to make sure that it is a valid area number and if it
    isn't then the program will exit. It is ok if you don't enter any
    arguments if you like in this situation you are prompted for the above
    information with the added advantage that the program will bring up a
    list of all library areas on your BBS with the area numbers to help
    choose the area which needs updating.

        Another use for Sysops would be to have the system automatically
    update your file lists at a set time every night using crontab or some
    other similar program and the command line switch '-O' for 
    overnight this will add the default comment to all files without a
    comment. This has the effect of bypassing the question asking for a
    description of the file.

        Will also create a list of the format filename.lzh
    Fullpath:filename.lzh for use as a magic files list. I don't know how
    useful this is to you but if you don't use it just delete it. This
    file is only created if you use the '-O' overnight switch 
    although this may change at a later date.

        Possible things to add in the future are if using the overnight
    switch for the program to create a list of files that need there
    comment fields updated. Program to create a master list of all files in
    all file librarys. Lists sorted by date newest at the top of the list,
    or oldest at the top. Maybe even a user definable sort using an
    environment variable. I have lots of ideas but if you can think of
    something that you would like that is not on the above list then drop
    me a line.

